TITLE
-----
Migrate authentication to Supabase Auth and database to PostgreSQL


DESCRIPTION
-----------
Replace Keycloak + MySQL with Supabase Auth + PostgreSQL across all backend
services and the Next.js frontend. Backend services switch from the Keycloak
Admin Client library to direct HTTP calls via Spring RestClient against the
Supabase Admin Auth API. All four data services replace mysql-connector-j with
the PostgreSQL driver. Core-banking Flyway migrations are rewritten for PostgreSQL
syntax. Docker-compose removes Keycloak and MySQL containers and adds a local
PostgreSQL container with Supabase env-var overrides. The frontend replaces
NextAuth KeycloakProvider with a Credentials provider backed by Supabase.


ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
-------------------
- [x] KeycloakManager, KeycloakProperties, KeycloakUserService removed from user-service
- [x] SupabaseProperties and SupabaseAuthService created in user-service
- [x] UserService updated to use SupabaseAuthService
- [x] internet-banking-user-service build passes
- [x] core-banking-service: flyway-mysql removed, postgresql added, migrations rewritten
- [x] core-banking-service build passes
- [x] internet-banking-fund-transfer-service: mysql replaced with postgresql; build passes
- [x] internet-banking-utility-payment-service: mysql replaced with postgresql; build passes
- [x] docker-compose: keycloak + MySQL removed; postgres_app_db added; env vars set
- [x] Frontend: email/password login form; Supabase credentials provider; package.json updated
- [x] Build passes: ./gradlew clean build (for each affected service)


